
`native/` holds the AUnit tests for ImplementPlanter/InterfacePlanter
(../lib/PootmachinebesturingCore/src/), run natively (no Teensy attached):

- `native/tests/` -- one `test_<ClassName>.cpp` per class under test.
- `native/support/` -- a small, self-contained set of Arduino-shaped stubs
  (Print/Stream/EEPROM/Arduino.h/etc.), not a real EpoxyDuino dependency, plus
  `native_main.cpp` (the host `int main()` entry point).
- `native/PootmachinebesturingNativeTests.cpp` -- the single AUnit driver
  (`setup()`/`loop()`), matching Ploegbesturing's/Salacia's/Loofdoes'
  `PloegbesturingNativeTests.cpp`/`SalaciaNativeTests.cpp`/
  `LoofdoesNativeTests.cpp` pattern. Every `test_*.cpp` file only registers
  `test(...)` blocks; none of them define `setup()`/`loop()` themselves, so
  they all link into one combined binary instead of one binary per test file.
- `native/run_tests_msvc.ps1` -- MSVC fallback for Windows without GCC.

```
pio run -e native
.pio/build/native/program(.exe)
```

Needs a real host C++17 compiler on PATH (g++ or clang++) -- on Windows
without one, use test\native\run_tests_msvc.ps1 instead, which builds and
runs the same combined binary via MSVC directly. That script passes
`/Zc:preprocessor` -- MSVC's legacy preprocessor mishandles AUnit's
`test(SuiteName, testName)` argument-count dispatch, which every test in
this project uses (matching Ploegbesturing's/Salacia's/Loofdoes' convention:
groups each test's display name under the class it exercises, e.g.
`ImplementPlanter_position_ascendingCalibration_atPoint0`,
`InterfacePlanter_update_staleGgaFix_selectsHold`).

## Known gaps

- `CalibrationPlanter` (the LCD/button calibration wizard extracted from the
  legacy `InterfacePlanter::Calibrate()`) is `#ifdef ARDUINO`-guarded and
  deliberately excluded from `[env:native]`'s `build_src_filter` -- it drives
  real LCD/button hardware through a sequence of blocking `while(true)` menu
  loops, the same shape of problem Ploegbesturing's `CalibrationPlough` and
  Loofdoes' `CalibrationSprayer` have, and which is excluded there for the
  same reason. No native coverage exists or is planned for it.
- `InterfacePlanter::UpdateScreen()` (LCD rendering) compiles as part of
  `InterfacePlanter.cpp` (needed since `CheckButtons()`/`Update()`, which
  *are* tested, live in the same file) but its output isn't asserted on by
  any test -- `test/native/support/InterfaceI2CLCD.hpp`'s `WriteBuffer`/
  `WriteScreen` are no-ops.
- The `teensy41` real-board env (ACAN_T4-based CAN/ISOBUS setup in
  `src/main.cpp`) has not been build-verified on real hardware -- only via
  `pio run -e teensy41`'s cross-compile in this environment.
- Only the `teensy41` board is wired up today. This module's legacy code
  (the combined Ploeg-Poot sketch) has historically also referenced Arduino
  Uno, Arduino Micro, and a Teensy 3.5/3.6 protoboard -- their pin-config
  `#ifdef` branches remain in `ConfigPlanter.hpp`/`ConfigImplementPlanter.hpp`/
  `ConfigInterfacePlanter.hpp` for future revival, but none of them has a
  buildable `platformio.ini` env yet.
- `xteAvg`/`dxte` (private `ImplementPlanter` members, kept in step with the
  legacy `xte_avg`/`dxte` fields for calibration/debug parity) have no public
  getter and so aren't directly asserted on by any test; `setSetpoint()`'s
  effect on `setpoint`/`GetPosition()` is covered instead, through
  `Update()`.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing (not used here -- pio test's
own Unity-based runner doesn't understand this project's AUnit setup):
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html
